{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling","id":551566,"title":"The Greastest Horror in Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T08:33:13-07:00","id":551566,"title":"The Greastest Horror in Changeling","content":"The thing that gave Changeling it's greatest force of Horror were the Sidhe. The game showed how irresponsible dreams create horror, misery, injustice, and cruelty. Because the Sidhe were dreams of power, the power of beauty, the power of wealth, the power of social prestige, power without responsibility or compassion, they were lovely monsters.<br /> <br /> Remember the Sidhe have no idea that they're being selfish. Much like the nobles of Europe and other lands they can't imagine why people don't just obey them, and see those who say no or simply don't want to be bothered as evil or mad. Watching the film <b>Savages</b>, the Selma Hyack character was a perfect sidhe noble. She demands that the protagonists give up their freedom and serve her as expendable pawns in an organization that will look down on them as mere scum. She is upset that they don't simply throw their personal freedom and security away for her whim and is physically and psychologically brutal to them for daring to resist. Her sevant, played by Benicio del Toro, dismisses the protagonists as savages for not following his prudish and brutal code, but sees raping O as proof of his manliness. A totally sidhe style of behavior.<br /> <br /> The sidhe see themselves as being like the French nobles in <b>The Scarlet Primpernell</b>. Victims desperately fighting for survival. But the Sidhe behave more like the Count de Evermont in <b>Tale of Two Cities.</b> This comes from the simple fact that the sidhe can't form much real sympathy with anyone who isn't a sidhe. The problem of the Norse Sidhe (must look up the name) is the extreme, but no sidhe on record really gets a non-sidhe.<br /> <br /> (I'll post more later, soon)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-15-2015, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T19:02:23-07:00","id":552466,"title":"","content":"While certain sidhe could definitely be horrific, I'd hardly call them the central horror of Changeling. The true darkness of Changeling is that no matter what you do, no matter what you accomplish, you are doomed forget it and you're true nature. No one will ever know what kind of life you lived.<br /> <br /> It's actually something that hits me a lot harder these days than when I was playing the game back in its heyday. The past several years I've had to watch as Alzheimer's has slowly taken my grandmother. Now days, her body is there, but she just isn't. Believe me, that's some gut wrenching, horrific stuff, and it's the fate of every single changeling. The lucky ones are the who go out in a blaze of glory fighting some monster or an evil sidhe ruler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:37:53-07:00","id":554681,"title":"","content":"Botched post the system forces me to leave in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-14-2015, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:40:11-07:00","id":554683,"title":"","content":"Remember , the Dreaming favors the Sidhe. Their dreams, their myths, their whims, devour your life and achievement. It's like being the kid who earned valedictorian finding everybody talking about the Captain of the football team getting a scholarship to a bigger school than the valedictorian could ever hope for.<br /> <br /> Remember most bullies are in fact the popular kids. The victims of bullies are more likely to be expelled than bullies ever are. The Authority figures in schools almost always identify with the bullies and loath the victims. In many ways <b>Changeling: The Dreaming</b> is about being creative kids in high School. The Sidhe are the champions of Banality, as well as the beauty Queens and team captains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-15-2015, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:30:24-07:00","id":554874,"title":"","content":"Sidhe. The word is <b>Sidhe</b>. A shide is a thin board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:43:27-07:00","id":555049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=554683#post554683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shide are the champions of Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading stuff that's just not there. The sidhe have just as much capacity for heroism and villainy as any other kith. On top of that, just because a changeling occupies the role of villain, doesn't mean they're an agent of banality. Stories need both heroes and villains to exist. The seelie and unseelie courts are both equally glamourous. Banality is being in a rut, choosing comfort and familiarity over fulfilling one's potential. Evil characters shake things up, get people to aspire to something greater, *feel* something. There's plenty of glamour to be had there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:38:40-07:00","id":555092,"title":"","content":"You can't be a knight going to rescue the princess if nobody sequester her to begin with...<br /> <br /> Stories need antagonists as much as heroes, and both, Noble Shide and Commoner, can (and do) play these roles. Changeling understand the need of evil, so the Dreaming can live, much like in the neverending story both heroes and villains fear the &quot;nothingness&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, no, nothing about the Sidhe sounds particularly banal to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their dreams, their myths, their whims, devour your life and achievement.</div> </div> </div> </div>XDXD, I HAVE to remember to put that phrase in the mouth of a learned Technocrat or Daedalean when speaking about Fae in general","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-14-2015, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:40:14-07:00","id":555093,"title":"","content":"You and Pooka should ready my thing about modernizing Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:44:29-07:00","id":555361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=554683#post554683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember , the Dreaming favors the Shide. Their dreams, their myths, their whims, devour your life and achievement. It's like being the kid who earned valedictorian finding everybody talking about the Captain of the football team getting a scholarship to a bigger school than the valedictorian could ever hope for. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more the fate of enchanted humans, actually. Vulnerable to all of the Dreaming's dangers, but without a drop of magic to protect themselves. Their noses pressed against the window, able to see the &quot;cool kid's party&quot; . . .but never able to go in and have fun themselves. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In many ways <b>Changeling: The Dreaming</b> is about creative kids in high School. The Shide are the champions of Banality. </div> </div> </div>You're half right. The sidhe aren't champions of Banality - they're fae born of human stories about knights and royalty. The evil usurper who murders the rightful king, and institutes a horrific reign of terror and oppression. The rightful heir who overthrows him, with the aid of a plucky band of misfits. A couple who fall madly in love, but cannot be together, because they belong to two warring noble houses (<i>a la</i> Romeo and Juliet). . . These are all examples of sidhe. And not of that's banal. <br /> <br /> But you are right about the &quot;creative kids in high school&quot; idea. They may have a world-changing novel in them, or a fantastic new style of painting. But most of them will never get a chance to explore their talents. Or their work will be a commercial failure, and they'll have to restock shelves for Walmart, just to pay the bills. Banality isn't supernatural evil. Dark wizards sacrificing virgins, dark knights tormenting peasants, ogres eating children . . that's all right out of myths and legends - and thus part of the Dreaming. <br /> <br /> Banality . . . Banality is the dead-eyed looked of a bureaucrat who hates their job, and is just going through the motions, calling &quot;next&quot; as they work through the line of applicants. Banality is staying in your hometown, and becoming an accountant, rather than chase your dream of being a rock star (or actress, or astronaut). Shelving that amazing idea, because its &quot;just not practical&quot;. Its mindless routine, conformity, drudgery. Its losing yourself in the cycle of paying bills, holding down a 9-to-5, and making sure the kids get to their dance classes and basketball practices. Of letting yourself become just a cog in the machine, when you could have been &quot;the one&quot;. <br /> <br /> So, just as most of the creative kids in high school will never be able to realize their dreams, finding something more &quot;practical&quot; . . .and maybe accepting a half-assessed substitute (singing in the church choir, or being in community theater), most changelings will fail, too. For every changeling who manages to find enough glamour to hold on to themselves indefinitely, to stay young, beautiful and magical forever, a thousand are going to grow old and forget. <br /> <br /> And most fall hard. Spending your life slaying dragons and rescuing princesses doesn't exactly bring in the big bucks. Nor does it look good on a modern resume. Many end up on the streets, or in insane asylums. And a changeling consumed by Banality can't even hold to the memories of their adventures - in fact, many come to look back on their youthful &quot;goofing off&quot; as irresponsible . . .even with some loathing. <br /> <br /> That's the horror of <i>Changeling</i>. To have actually ridden unicorns in a faerie forest, and seen the majesty of a flight of dragons rage across the sky . . . only to grow old, and believe that none of it ever actually happened. And worse, to know that one day - if you live long enough - you'll be the old geezer yelling at kids to stop fantasizing about such foolish things. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:17:08-07:00","id":555710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=554874#post554874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidhe. The word is <b>Sidhe</b>. A shide is a thin board.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, my spelling is subnormal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:27:04-07:00","id":555719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=555092#post555092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XDXD, I HAVE to remember to put that phrase in the mouth of a learned Technocrat or Daedalean when speaking about Fae in general</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocrats take the worst examples of any group and define the whole by them. I'm looking at how the Sidhe worked in just about every single book of C:tD and building from there. Their is very little in the game as it is published to suggest that the Sidhe have ever been anything but a brutal burden to the Commoners and a plague on the Dreamers. Where do you find one thing the Sidhe did that was worthy, decent, and generous? The Sidhe woke up after centuries is paradise, walked out into the waking world, and demanded everybody be their slave. They are no more or less brutal and greedy than the elder vampires, true. But are the elder Vampires worthy of emulation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:33:14-07:00","id":555723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=555093#post555093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and Pooka should ready my thing about modernizing Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find it. Kick it to the top and I'll look into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:53:22-07:00","id":555747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=555719#post555719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you find one thing the Sidhe did that was worthy, decent, and generous?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Changeling: The Dreaming 1st edition</li> <li>Changeling: The Dreaming 2nd edition</li> <li>Book of Lost Dreams</li> <li>Players Guide to Changeling: The Dreaming</li> <li>Immortal Eyes: The Toybox</li> <li>Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill</li> <li>Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings</li> <li>Isle of the Mighty</li> <li>Kingdom of Willows</li> <li>Nobles: The Shining Host</li> <li>Noblesse Oblige: The Book of Houses</li> <li>Pour L'Amour et Liberte: The Book of Houses 2</li> <li>Book of Lost Houses: The Second Coming</li> <li>War in Concordia</li> </ul>Even Fool's Luck: Way of the Commoner which is specifically anti-noble propaganda still has one heroic and sympathetic sidhe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:11:56-07:00","id":556863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=555747#post555747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even Fool's Luck: Way of the Commoner which is specifically anti-noble propaganda still has one heroic and sympathetic sidhe.</div> </div> </div> </div>A device that showed how commonplace Noble brutality was. <b>Nobles aren't</b> gets it right. Sure some noble think well of themselves, the Sidhe are the heroes of the story, and they insist that it be every story. But good press doesn't equal virtue. Look at the opposite case, the USA is normally characterized as being ten thousand times worse than Nazi Germany or Stalinist Russia, but are we, in reality any way near as bad as either of those? Is the fact we are slandered proof of our vices? Similarly, is the Dreaming enforced, and brutally enforced, praise of the Sidhe, any proof of their virtue? Or is it simply their role in a story? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:53:57-07:00","id":556885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=556863#post556863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A device that showed how commonplace Noble brutality was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just blatant propaganda, especially when you realize that most of the horrors the book describes being committed with Sovereign are actually impossible to do with Sovereign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:45:00-07:00","id":558416,"title":"","content":"With <b>Sovereign</b> as it now exists after decades in the normal world. It's clear that when they first returned the Sidhe had a great deal of power from Arcadia backing them up. I assume that Arts and Realms, not known in the waking world, boosted their power during the return. Besides, where are the counter stories of Sidhe selflessness, virtue, and responsible behavior. They only come from sidhe propagandists. The mean spirited treatment of House Scatach gives the game away. For being Responsible first and foremost, Scatach is despised. Note: House Gwydion 's treatment of both Liam and Beaumayn. The houses Liam and Beaumayn both chose duty, and Gwydion brutally punished both for it. And Gwydion is supposed to be the Seelie House par excellence. Gwydion, supposed to be the purest champions of Honor, show more contempt for honor than either Balor or Alil.<br /> <br /> Further points on the Sidhe as sources of horror. House Leanhaun wants to make the Earth into a living hell. True they are trying to break the mad brutal curse of House Gwydion on them, but they plan to sacrafice billions to break the curse. Moreover, Gwydion set up the curse so that only the most monstrous evils possible could break it!<br /> <br /> Almost all the Sidhe who comment on mortal government either say that Humanity needs to be enslaved to the Sidhe or they strongly favor a return to the horrors of absolute monarchy.<br /> <br /> Come on, the Sidhe, as written up in Changeling the Dreaming, are vermin!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-17-2015, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T00:13:08-07:00","id":559123,"title":"","content":"it seems as though your oversimplifying the situation a bit. the sidhe are not a hive mind or one entity. they are an entire race of faerie, that yes have and continue to do horrible things. So do the redcaps and slugha, so do pooka and boggans. even trolls have been known to do horrible things to people and other fae not because they are any of those things, but because people with inhuman desires and power comes a predilection toward corruption and tragedy. there are just as many heroic sidhe as there are villainous ones, just by virtue of them being people rather than objects. this is the world of darkness and things are not always as simple as they seem, especially in changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T01:38:05-07:00","id":559147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=558416#post558416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With <b>Sovereign</b> as it now exists after decades in the normal world. It's clear that when they first returned the Sidhe had a great deal of power from Arcadia backing them up. I assume that Arts and Realms, not known in the waking world, boosted their power during the return. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, they were also horribly vulnerable to banality at that point, too. There are comments sprinkled throughout the game (starting with <i>Nobles: the Shining Host</i>) that the first wave of returning sidhe were virtually cut off from modern technology. Simply riding a motorcycle, or in a car, could be fatal.<br /> <br /> So while the sidhe initially had a magical advantage, they were denied the fruits of modern Western society. Which the commoner changelings took full advantage of (think &quot;assault rifles with iron bullets&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, where are the counter stories of Sidhe selflessness, virtue, and responsible behavior. They only come from sidhe propagandists.The mean spirited treatment of House Scatach gives the game away. For being Responsible first and foremost, Scatach is despised. Note: House Gwydion 's treatment of both Liam and Beaumayn. The houses Liam and Beaumayn both chose duty, and Gwydion brutally punished both for it.. . . </div> </div> </div>Well, Scathach, Liam, and Baumayn are sidhe, too. So if you're saying they're good and honorable, and criticizing Gwydion for mistreating them . . .<br /> <br /> And even many of the more radical commoner fae supported High King David (most definitely a sidhe) as a just and fair monarch. Some would've preferred a more . . . republican system, but you'd be hard pressed to find someone saying he's corrupt, or doing a bad job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Almost all the Sidhe who comment on mortal government either say that Humanity needs to be enslaved to the Sidhe or they strongly favor a return to the horrors of absolute monarchy. </div> </div> </div>Well . . .yeah. The sidhe are born of humanity's myths and legends about <i>knights and royalty</i>. Somewhere in the Dreaming, there are probably fae born of the dreams of democracy and human rights . . .but they haven't shown up yet.<br /> <br /> And just because most of the sidhe support the idea of monarchy, doesn't make them bad. Because they're fae, they don't &quot;do&quot; mediocrity and incompetence. If a &quot;good guy&quot; sidhe comes to power, he's going to be a living embodiment of humanity's stories of the best kings and nobles. Brave as Arthur or Charlemagne, wise as Solomon, deeply compassionate . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:55:33-07:00","id":559325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=559123#post559123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems as though your oversimplifying the situation a bit. the sidhe are not a hive mind or one entity. they are an entire race of faerie, that yes have and continue to do horrible things. So do the redcaps and slugha, so do pooka and boggans. even trolls have been known to do horrible things to people and other fae not because they are any of those things, but because people with inhuman desires and power comes a predilection toward corruption and tragedy. there are just as many heroic sidhe as there are villainous ones, just by virtue of them being people rather than objects. this is the world of darkness and things are not always as simple as they seem, especially in changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But, as written in the books, the Sidhe do vile things, but never have a counterbalancing virtue. Further, the Sidhe are like many real world bullies, the beautiful people who have their collective sadism excused because of their beauty. It's a proven real world fact that people with beauty and status (the defining traits of the Sidhe) routinely have their vices excused, their cruelties laughed off, and extra chances in plenty. The Sidhe are the nightmare side of humanity and the Dreaming's love of Physical Beauty even when it comes with total moral ugliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:04:39-07:00","id":559339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=559147#post559147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, they were also horribly vulnerable to banality at that point, too. There are comments sprinkled throughout the game (starting with <i>Nobles: the Shining Host</i>) that the first wave of returning sidhe were virtually cut off from modern technology. Simply riding a motorcycle, or in a car, could be fatal.<br /> <br /> So while the sidhe initially had a magical advantage, they were denied the fruits of modern Western society. Which the commoner changelings took full advantage of (think &quot;assault rifles with iron bullets&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>If people were trying to enslave me and my family I'd get bitter and nasty fighting them. The sidhe came as imperialists and conquistidores, they pretended to no mercy or decency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, Scathach, Liam, and Baumayn are sidhe, too. So if you're saying they're good and honorable, and criticizing Gwydion for mistreating them . . .<br /> <br /> And even many of the more radical commoner fae supported High King David (most definitely a sidhe) as a just and fair monarch. Some would've preferred a more . . . republican system, but you'd be hard pressed to find someone saying he's corrupt, or doing a bad job. </div> </div> </div>My point was the selfish and dangerous ways they treat even each other. House Gwydion turned House Leanhaun into a weapon to destroy the world, and did so on a whim. And if you put Arthur Pendragon on a throne and made him King of America I would still take up arms against him. I love the tales of Arthur, but absolute monarchs don't belong in the modern world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well . . .yeah. The sidhe are born of humanity's myths and legends about <i>knights and royalty</i>. Somewhere in the Dreaming, there are probably fae born of the dreams of democracy and human rights . . .but they haven't shown up yet.<br /> <br /> And just because most of the sidhe support the idea of monarchy, doesn't make them bad. Because they're fae, they don't &quot;do&quot; mediocrity and incompetence. If a &quot;good guy&quot; sidhe comes to power, he's going to be a living embodiment of humanity's stories of the best kings and nobles. Brave as Arthur or Charlemagne, wise as Solomon, deeply compassionate . . . </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the dreams of childhood can cripple you as an adult. Monarchy and the dream of the <b>Good King</b> failed, and they still fail. Would you want to live in North Korea? Saudi Arabia? The Commoners moved on, now they are stagnated against their wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-02-2025, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T15:36:52-07:00","id":594201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=556885#post556885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just blatant propaganda, especially when you realize that most of the horrors the book describes being committed with Sovereign are actually impossible to do with Sovereign.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was wrong with the Sovereign used in Fool's Luck? (Has never used Sovereign...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T18:34:28-07:00","id":594316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=555092#post555092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't be a knight going to rescue the princess if nobody sequester her to begin with...<br /> <br /> Stories need antagonists as much as heroes, and both, Noble Shide and Commoner, can (and do) play these roles. Changeling understand the need of evil, so the Dreaming can live, much like in the neverending story both heroes and villains fear the &amp;quot;nothingness&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> So, no, nothing about the Sidhe sounds particularly banal to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: </div> </div> </div> </div>*Winces* Your perspective in some sense IS the correct one, but that is because the game is somewhat schizophrenic and not completely thought out. <br /> <br /> First of all, the Unseelie, at least in theory, aren't bad guys just like the Seelie aren't supposed to be good guys. The writers botched that up horribly fluff wise , but it's still true according to the game. <br /> <br /> And the Sidhe ARE Banal. It happens with the Fae. Remember how, in DREAMS AND NIGHTMARES, a commune of Changelings living in the Dreaming were actually killing their part of the Dreaming just by being boring? The Sidhe are arrogance incarnate, for the most part, and they have a pretty sweet deal for so long as they can maintain the status quo. Watch COSMOS, specifically that one episode where the Big Lead put up a fight to keep making money long after it was proven they were poisoning the planet. Do you think the Sidhe are really going to promote change and progress any more than the privileged in our world? <br /> <br /> And the Sidhe ARE the privileged. They did nothing to earn their crowns, unlike the Trolls who stood by the commoners and sheltered them after their Sidhe &quot;rightful&quot; rulers abandoned them. Sure, the Dreaming favors them, but how much of that is due to the Tuatha Da'Naan? Their like a bunch of super spoiled trust fund babies who don't care about how many people are hungry on the streets where they live, or how many are wasting away in sweat shops making them their toys, as long as the life they have grown accustomed to is always there. And since I prefer to downplay the &quot;lost innocence of childhood&quot; aspect of Changeling, and given how in the real world there are few things more horrific and destructive to the human race and the planet than they apathy of the privileged people, I think the original poster is probably correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T20:28:55-07:00","id":594387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=555093#post555093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and Pooka should ready my thing about modernizing Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Linkies., please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T23:56:56-07:00","id":594528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=556863#post556863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A device that showed how commonplace Noble brutality was. <b>Nobles aren't</b> gets it right. Sure some noble think well of themselves, the Sidhe are the heroes of the story, and they insist that it be every story. But good press doesn't equal virtue. Look at the opposite case, the USA is normally characterized as being ten thousand times worse than Nazi Germany or Stalinist Russia, but are we, in reality any way near as bad as either of those? Is the fact we are slandered proof of our vices? Similarly, is the Dreaming enforced, and brutally enforced, praise of the Sidhe, any proof of their virtue? Or is it simply their role in a story?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of everything said, I choose this one.<br /> <br /> Lets see...<br /> <br /> First of all, USA ended earlier a war almost impossible to lose by a very honorable and ethic method. Launching the most heinous weapon ever created against two civil cities, with plans for more 7 bombs if Japan didn't surrendered. At least 129.000 and maybe more than 246.000 people, most of them civilians at home, died in 2 days. Had all the planned bombings hapened, USA would kill more people in nine days than Nazi Germany killed in five years (eleven million if considered both jews and non-jews).<br /> <br /> Those are facts. If you say they don't resume the entire story, you're pretty right. But they're true, nonetheless. USA &quot;War on Terror&quot; killed more than terrorism itself could hope to kill in american territory. And a lot of those deaths are of common people. But you're fighting for democracy, right!?<br /> <br /> Doesn't really matter how you answer it, or if you actualy believe USA to be good in the end. Hitler saved Germany from an economical crisis without equal. Japan rised from the ashes as a tecnological potency with a stable economy that don't even pretend to be a free economy (in Japan monopoly is a STATE policy, selected businesses are protected by the government).<br /> <br /> You ARE oversimplifying things. And you're doing it for the worst reason. REAL LIFE IDEOLOGY. You are forcing into the setting the idea that the guys who go against your ideology are by definition bad guys, and ignoring any reasoning on the other side, because you don't want to see your ideological enemies as redeemable. That's a shame...<br /> <br /> Most than other kiths, Sidhe are ANACHRONISMS. Yeah, now we live in the world after French Revolution. Libert\u00e9, \u00e9galit\u00e9, fraternit\u00e9. We had grown accostumed to these ideals for 2 centuries right now. Even in places like England and Spain, where they still have monarchs, the major power is a parliament.<br /> <br /> But Changelings are dreams that roamed Europe during the eleventh century. Back in those days, NO ONE thought monarchy to be a bad thing. It isn't because the nobles never liked common people or where indiferent to their needs. Of course, probably a lot of nobles where like that. But even the most kind and well meaning just couldn't THINK of a different system. If things where so simple, we would have such a lot earlier...<br /> <br /> In that context, the Sidhe are precisely that: unable to think of a system without nobility. They are dreams OF nobility. To remove nobility from the picture is just freaking ALIEN to them. Some of them see the suffering of others. And they try what they can to ease this suffering. But they CAN'T do that by casting aside nobility, because this is ingrained in their nature. And yes, they CAN be kind, empathic and selfless.<br /> <br /> At least if you understand kindness, like normal people do, as wishing health and happiness for other people. Something that YOU can think is only possible in a democracy, but isn't DEFINED as democracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T02:53:25-07:00","id":594600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=558416#post558416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With <b>Sovereign</b> as it now exists after decades in the normal world. It's clear that when they first returned the Sidhe had a great deal of power from Arcadia backing them up. I assume that Arts and Realms, not known in the waking world, boosted their power during the return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except soveriegn had been on earth for the centuries of the interregnum. It wasn't COMMON, but it certainly wasn't some Sidhe-only art lost to Arcadia for all that time. That said, Sovereign 5 <i>certainly can</i> accomplish some of the groady things mentioned in Fool's Luck. And I woudl agree that the returning sidhe probably had <i>way</i> more people whoi had mastered Sovereign to that level than the opposition did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, where are the counter stories of Sidhe selflessness, virtue, and responsible behavior. They only come from sidhe propagandists. </div> </div> </div>The word you want is &quot;protagonists&quot; actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mean spirited treatment of House Scatach gives the game away. For being Responsible first and foremost, Scatach is despised. </div> </div> </div>Scathach made an active choice ot abandon pretty much everything that defines them as sidhe. You can have a look at how Trolls treat their fellows who abandon their strength, or how redcaps treet Seelie redcaps, and see the same thing going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note: House Gwydion 's treatment of both Liam </div> </div> </div>Liam might have singlehandedly brought the inquisition down onto the fae. Oh, and he tried to murder another noble in his own hold. Over the love of a mortal woman. He was exiled, and his House with him. Not <i>so</i> exiled that they didn't get to scurry back to Arcadia during the shattering, mind...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and Beaumayn. </div> </div> </div>Didja miss the part where the Beaumayn were abducting fae and ritually sacrificing them with cold iron, with the only defense being &quot;trust us, this is going to be awesome&quot;? ...While admitting they didn't actually know if it was going to be awesome or not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The houses Liam and Beaumayn both chose duty, and Gwydion brutally punished both for it. </div> </div> </div>The houses were punished for gross crimes perpetrated against the fae as a whole. And considerign what human justice does in these instances, tmporary semi-exile and nasty names are a pretty light punishment for what htey were doing (especially since, i nthe case of the beaumayn, some are still doing it...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Gwydion is supposed to be the Seelie House par excellence. Gwydion, supposed to be the purest champions of Honor, show more contempt for honor than either Balor or Alil. </div> </div> </div>Seelie doesn't mean nice. It does embrace honor. Buuuut honor can be brutal, mean, and painfully shoirt-sighted. No one would call Ned Stark of Winterfell anything less than greatly honorable. and that stalwart honor utterly destroyed his family, threw the kingdom into a terrible war, and might result in the land being overrun with smurfs who make snow sculptures out of corpses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further points on the Sidhe as sources of horror. House Leanhaun wants to make the Earth into a living hell. True they are trying to break the mad brutal curse of House Gwydion on them, but they plan to sacrafice billions to break the curse. Moreover, Gwydion set up the curse so that only the most monstrous evils possible could break it! </div> </div> </div>Actually it was a member of House Liam that levied the curse on Leanhaun. And yup, Leanhaun's plans are kinda insane. Good sources of horror, of a particular sort.if you want that cthulhu kind of vibe in your game, leanhaun are probably better antgonists than Balor - first, everyon <i>expects</i> Balor... and two, the Balor expect to be in charge at the end, while leanhaun are more like &quot;screw it, so long as we break the curse we'll take whatever.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Almost all the Sidhe who comment on mortal government either say that Humanity needs to be enslaved to the Sidhe or they strongly favor a return to the horrors of absolute monarchy. </div> </div> </div>Well, because the world they <i>left</i> followed those outlines and was, for the most part, functional. They come back, see a world that is clearly absolutely DYSFUNCTIONAL, and has an entirely different standard of governance. Clearly things were better with the old ways, and <i>of course</i> the sidhe are the rightful custodians of such a return. And you know what? A majority of commoners feel more or less the same way. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Come on, the Sidhe, as written up in Changeling the Dreaming, are vermin! </div> </div> </div>Somewhat. But then so are the Ventrue, Silver Fangs, and Order of Hermes, as written. You haveto develop a filter for the WoD's habit of creating a &quot;powers that be&quot; faction, and then setting the entire rest of the game's populace against that particular splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T03:13:51-07:00","id":594605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=594316#post594316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Sidhe ARE Banal. It happens with the Fae. Remember how, in DREAMS AND NIGHTMARES, a commune of Changelings living in the Dreaming were actually killing their part of the Dreaming just by being boring? The Sidhe are arrogance incarnate, for the most part, and they have a pretty sweet deal for so long as they can maintain the status quo. Watch COSMOS, specifically that one episode where the Big Lead put up a fight to keep making money long after it was proven they were poisoning the planet. Do you think the Sidhe are really going to promote change and progress any more than the privileged in our world?</div> </div> </div> </div>You would have a good point... if the Sidhe were a unified front.<br /> <br /> They're not. Not by a long shot. The Houses are in open competition against each other. Even if htey are &quot;allied.&quot; The five core &quot;Seelie&quot; houses are always ramming agaisnt each other, jockying for position and power. Ailil, Leanhaun, and Balor are allies of opportunity, and all three have plans to dispose of the other two after the Seelie are toppled. The scathach <i>claim</i> to seek no title, but oh oops, here come a bunch of Arcadian scathach who are more than happy to do just that. And with them come four other houses that really just confuse the heck out of everyone else (An unseelie house that makes Gwydion look like honorless pantswetters? A tooth-achingly seelie house that thinks cold iron is fun? Why are there russian sidhe? <i>What's going on?!</i>) who are <i>also</i> making power plays.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the Seelie vs. Unseelie competition... and when you remember that sidhe can swap courts like nothing (unless they're Balor, but who cares about Balor) <i>that</i> mess gets crazy fast.<br /> <br /> And then you reel in all the various personal plots, the alliances and oaths and connections and what have you... And you have a society that is <i>anything</i> but static or stagnant. Sire, &quot;The Sidhe&quot; all want to have positions of power and privilege... and hte best way to get it is to keep that other idhe over there from getting it. Or to devise a way around him somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Sidhe ARE the privileged. They did nothing to earn their crowns, unlike the Trolls who stood by the commoners and sheltered them after their Sidhe &quot;rightful&quot; rulers abandoned them. Sure, the Dreaming favors them, but how much of that is due to the Tuatha Da'Naan? Their like a bunch of super spoiled trust fund babies who don't care about how many people are hungry on the streets where they live, or how many are wasting away in sweat shops making them their toys, as long as the life they have grown accustomed to is always there. And since I prefer to downplay the &quot;lost innocence of childhood&quot; aspect of Changeling, and given how in the real world there are few things more horrific and destructive to the human race and the planet than they apathy of the privileged people, I think the original poster is probably correct. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Trolls&quot; no more earned it than &quot;The sidhe.&quot; Some of both were certainly generous and dutiful. others were simply bullies who took what they wanted and the people being taken from had no say in the matter - Realistically it's as hard to argue with an eight-foot dude poking a sword the size of a tree in your face, as it is to argue with skinny elf playing you with sovereign. They just involve different dice rolls on the part of the person jerking you around, is all. <i>Fools Luck</i> even mentions bands of trolls and redcaps effectively taking over freeholds by becoming &quot;guards&quot; - and then charging admission. And remember, it was the Troll's decision to bend knee to King David that ended the accordance war - and there are lots of commoners who trust trolls about as far as they can throw them, because of that. If they have nothing but nice things to say about trolls, it's quite likely do to being scared out of their spit by the prospect of actually getting a troll upset and being turned into a boggan-scented smear on the freehold wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T04:39:25-07:00","id":594632,"title":"","content":"I have no opinion on the matter. I'm just so excited to see people talking about and playing Changeling again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T05:22:06-07:00","id":594654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=594632#post594632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no opinion on the matter. I'm just so excited to see people talking about and playing Changeling again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T12:18:23-07:00","id":594910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=594528#post594528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of everything said, I choose this one.<br /> <br /> Lets see...<br /> <br /> First of all, USA ended earlier a war almost impossible to lose by a very honorable and ethic method. Launching the most heinous weapon ever created against two civil cities, with plans for more 7 bombs if Japan didn't surrendered. At least 129.000 and maybe more than 246.000 people, most of them civilians at home, died in 2 days. Had all the planned bombings hapened, USA would kill more people in nine days than Nazi Germany killed in five years (eleven million if considered both jews and non-jews).</div> </div> </div> </div>Your numbers are wildly off. also remember that the two A-bombings killed fewer people than <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanking_Massacre\" target=\"_blank\">rape of Nanking</a>. You've been taught that America is the great Satan so long you think the Japanese Imperialists were saints.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those are facts. If you say they don't resume the entire story, you're pretty right. But they're true, nonetheless. USA &quot;War on Terror&quot; killed more than terrorism itself could hope to kill in american territory. And a lot of those deaths are of common people. But you're fighting for democracy, right!? </div> </div> </div>Is it ISIS, Al-Qaeda, Assad, or Sadam, you see as the better path than democracy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doesn't really matter how you answer it, or if you actualy believe USA to be good in the end. Hitler saved Germany from an economical crisis without equal. Japan rised from the ashes as a tecnological potency with a stable economy that don't even pretend to be a free economy (in Japan monopoly is a STATE policy, selected businesses are protected by the government).<br /> <br /> You ARE oversimplifying things. And you're doing it for the worst reason. REAL LIFE IDEOLOGY. You are forcing into the setting the idea that the guys who go against your ideology are by definition bad guys, and ignoring any reasoning on the other side, because you don't want to see your ideological enemies as redeemable. That's a shame... </div> </div> </div>I live in the 21st century were my nation is defined as simply evil and any form of government that isn't democracy is exalted as the great new truth. I don't like the notion that ancient evils as foul as any Vampire Lord should be held to be virtue incarnate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More than most other kiths, Sidhe are ANACHRONISMS. Yeah, now we live in the world after French Revolution. Libert\u00e9, \u00e9galit\u00e9, fraternit\u00e9. We had grown accostumed to these ideals for 2 centuries right now. Even in places like England and Spain, where they still have monarchs, the major power is a parliament.<br /> <br /> But Changelings are dreams that roamed Europe during the eleventh century. Back in those days, NO ONE thought monarchy to be a bad thing. It isn't because the nobles never liked common people or where indiferent to their needs. Of course, probably a lot of nobles where like that. But even the most kind and well meaning just couldn't THINK of a different system. If things where so simple, we would have such a lot earlier...<br /> <br /> In that context, the Sidhe are precisely that: unable to think of a system without nobility. They are dreams OF nobility. To remove nobility from the picture is just freaking ALIEN to them. Some of them see the suffering of others. And they try what they can to ease this suffering. But they CAN'T do that by casting aside nobility, because this is ingrained in their nature. And yes, they CAN be kind, empathic and selfless.<br /> <br /> At least if you understand kindness, like normal people do, as wishing health and happiness for other people. Something that YOU can think is only possible in a democracy, but isn't DEFINED as democracy. </div> </div> </div>But I study history, my Masters is in History (I've several minor dyslexias that mar my writing and spelling, but I earned my Masters). Yes I am aware that virtue can flourish in many forms. But certain governmental forms warp virtue into monstrosity. Consider the inquisition's priests. They sought to be merciful. They tortured people until they confessed to whatever crime they were said to be guilty of. Confession meant they could go to heaven. The rack and the thumbscrew were the <b><i>simple</i></b> tools of their mercy.<br /> <br /> What good the Sidhe do is filtered through humanity's wounds. It manifests as infection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-02-2025, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T17:04:49-07:00","id":595124,"title":"","content":"You misinterpreted my words completely, tough I can't say I'm surprised.<br /> <br /> First I tried to show you that things don't work in maniqueist ways. I'm aware of the attrocities both Japan and China already comitted, both against each other and against other people. Even their own people. The Kamikaze soldiers, as an example, where far from volunteered nationalists. They where mostly young intelectuals that couldn't adequate to militar or patriotic life, despised by the same officials that would regard them as heroes in front of the people.<br /> <br /> USA played a key role in the Great War, and should France and England had payd attention to american emissaries, maybe Nazi-German could not had happened at all.<br /> <br /> I don't think the japanese where saints, nor that americans are evil. I think they are countries, where the majority of people just live their lifes and some take decisions. Sometimes, good decisions. Sometimes very bad decisions.<br /> <br /> And my numbers, I do admit I didn't went far, just used wikipedia. The same you did linked here, by the way, and your numbers also could be called wildly off. Are they? I don't know, and it doesn't change a thing. The bomb was heinous, but that doesn't mean all americans are evil. Just that in some point in history they did a very bad thing. Every country does that.<br /> <br /> So, I don't think that any of those is better than democracy. In fact, I do defend democracy. What I will never defend is the use of an ideology to justify attrocities. If I wasn't clear enough, the USA created way more terror on the Middle East than it where really on risk of suffer. And, again, it wasn't meant to say that everything US do is evil. I will not oversimpify things to the point of prejudice.<br /> <br /> No one, except by yourself, is saying that they are virtue incarnate. You're the maniqueist here, assuming that there are no shades of grey, just black or white. Sorry, but you're in the wrong setting here. WoD is all about shades of grey. I'm ALSO living in the 21st century, I'm ALSO in a democratic country, as are most of humanity nowadays. By the way, I fail to see where in the world you see so much people that prayses other forms of government. Because most of Europe is democratic, even if not allways republic. There are not even a single nation in the Americas that isn't a democracy, even if some are arguably not as much as they advertise. Most of Africa and Asia also are run as democracies. And if some of those countries just pay lip service to democracy, the very fact that they're doing so shows how much people value democracy.<br /> <br /> But tough I DO agree that being arystocratic mummies is something to point against the Sidhe, I fail to see any reason to think that for not being paragons of virtue should make them DEVOID of virtue. By the way, you're in the 21st century, I'm on the 21st century, but the Sidhe are new here, y'know?<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Inquisition wheren't a government form, it was a government policy. And, by the way, completely out of context.<br /> <br /> Well, all said and done, I doubt you will listen. I'm very aware that you'll just start again. You think a bunch of imaginary knights are evil for being knights in 90's New York? Go ahead. Far from the worst nightmare of Changeling to me. And just to close, if I tought USA where the evil incarnate, why would I be in an american forum, talking about an american game!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T18:04:26-07:00","id":595193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=595124#post595124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And just to close, if I tought USA where the evil incarnate, why would I be in an american forum, talking about an american game!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said. Part of the problem here in the USA is a revolting fixation on a golden past that never really existed. Part of this is due to the after effects of decades worth of steady Cold War propaganda, which actually merged in an odd way with our religion (thank YOU, religious-right). <br /> <br /> Facing the past is hard, thanks to our famous national arrogance, but it is inevitable. The demographics are changing, and the heritage that some want to defend is going to belong to a minority in the coming years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T21:40:00-07:00","id":595376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=594605#post594605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;The Trolls&quot; no more earned it than &quot;The sidhe.&quot; Some of both were certainly generous and dutiful. others were simply bullies who took what they wanted and the people being taken from had no say in the matter - Realistically it's as hard to argue with an eight-foot dude poking a sword the size of a tree in your face, as it is to argue with skinny elf playing you with sovereign. They just involve different dice rolls on the part of the person jerking you around, is all. <i>Fools Luck</i> even mentions bands of trolls and redcaps effectively taking over freeholds by becoming &quot;guards&quot; - and then charging admission. And remember, it was the Troll's decision to bend knee to King David that ended the accordance war - and there are lots of commoners who trust trolls about as far as they can throw them, because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There may have been some evil Trolls, but I am pretty sure it was written more than once that the Trolls have been the protectors of the Fae and stepped up to protecting the Commoners when the Sidhe ran out on them. The Trolls may be big, but the Player's Guide strongly suggests that's because they are the dreams of the ideal protector. The strong kid who does what is right and who fights off bullies and the like. The Sidhe are just the Tuatha De Danann's little bundles of joy that they left behind to inherit the world after the war with the Fomorians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-19-2015, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T03:02:22-07:00","id":595518,"title":"","content":"In a more white and black scenario it would be pretty accurate, but again, shades of grey. Tough it is unlikely that many Trolls are outright evil, their way to protect people can have heavy downsides in some cases, and be a lot brutish even when well-meaning.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe are dreams of nobility, so they're also protectors in a sense, by the way. The main function of the noble in the Dark Ages is to oversee and protect the land, be it in the name of the king, of the people, or of himself. Surely it gives way more avenues to be a big jerk, but doesn't demand such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T12:08:20-07:00","id":595836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=595518#post595518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a more white and black scenario it would be pretty accurate, but again, shades of grey. Tough it is unlikely that many Trolls are outright evil, their way to protect people can have heavy downsides in some cases, and be a lot brutish even when well-meaning.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe are dreams of nobility, so they're also protectors in a sense, by the way. The main function of the noble in the Dark Ages is to oversee and protect the land, be it in the name of the king, of the people, or of himself. Surely it gives way more avenues to be a big jerk, but doesn't demand such.</div> </div> </div> </div>But noble in what frame of reference? You said my worldview was rigidly black and white, however you seem to be unable to flex your mind around the problems at hand. One of the most toxic things in my nation is the way so many people in the South (I live in North Carolina and am descended both from slaveholders and abolitionists) hold onto a fantasy about the antebellum south. An anti-democratic fantasy much like that of the sidhe with their chivalric delusions. As an American, I get insulted and slammed for my nation's past. We are told of the importance of humility and get large does of humiliation. Americans can see the difference between these, our critics never have yet.<br /> <br /> If, as the play says, &quot;In dreams begin responsibility.&quot; then the Sidhe are a total abdication of responsibility on all levels. Much like the 14th century English lords that were the models of the Sherriff of Notingham, the Sidhe can't see why their desires aren't seen as normal, good and fine. Just as the nobles saw the rebellious peasants as inspired by the devil, so the Sidhe can only see the commoners as warped or sick. Just like the 19th century slave-holders who saw the desire of their slaves to run away as a mental illness, or present day Europeans like yourself who see all Americans who don't want to ritually humiliated 24/7 as right-wing goons, you avoid seeing that the critique has a point.<br /> <br /> The great horror of the Sidhe is the basis of tragedy, the moral blindness of good people. The Seelie Sidhe do have high ideals, but because they can not see that they are hundreds of years out of step with the times and that aristocracy is no longer valuable, this makes them promotes great evils because of a basic blindness. Just as the standard European view of Americans as worthless Nazi trash poisons the possibility of trans-Atlantic communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-07-2023, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:31:30-07:00","id":596214,"title":"","content":"First, I'm not european. I'm south american.<br /> <br /> Second, I said my frame of reference.<br /> <br /> Third, I'm just saying you can't use any of this to put everyone on the same bag. And you're still doing that.<br /> <br /> Forth, you're starting to do that not against fictional elfs, but against real people here, thank you very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:14:01-07:00","id":596808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=552466#post552466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While certain sidhe could definitely be horrific, I'd hardly call them the central horror of Changeling. The true darkness of Changeling is that no matter what you do, no matter what you accomplish, you are doomed forget it and you're true nature. No one will ever know what kind of life you lived.<br /> <br /> It's actually something that hits me a lot harder these days than when I was playing the game back in its heyday. The past several years I've had to watch as Alzheimer's has slowly taken my grandmother. Now days, her body is there, but she just isn't. Believe me, that's some gut wrenching, horrific stuff, and it's the fate of every single changeling. The lucky ones are the who go out in a blaze of glory fighting some monster or an evil sidhe ruler.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I agree, a lot of people liked to hate on classic Changeling because the artwork was more whimsical and happy than the rest of the series, but that is exactly what made it so heartbreaking to play a Changeling in my opinion. You start off with this sense of childish whimsy and imagination, and then you're slowly crushed by the passing of the ages and the demands of society as you come to maturity.It's the story of a child losing their innocence and becoming bitter, unimaginable people because the world doesn't work the way they thought it did. Even if you manage to retain your Changeling nature into adulthood or beyond, people aren't going to think you're cute or playful when you start swinging a pen at an invisible dragon, they are probably going to throw you into an asylum while you desperately try to provoke their imagination with grandiose tales of magic and wonder.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then, of course, there are the consequences for having lived as a supernatural in the first place. It doesn't matter if you forget what you are or if you become human again, you have been living among the supernatural societies for years and it is very likely you've made some enemies. Vampires, werewolves, mages and yes even the Sidhe, they're known to hold a grudge and now you have no special powers to defend yourself. Hell you might not even remember they exist anymore! Without your powers and memories, you are defenseless and they can strike at any time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Out of all the classic splats, Changeling is the one I would be least eager to play. Not because of the artwork or the peter pan style characters, but because the overarching theme of the game is depressing, which makes it a perfect addition to the World of Darkness!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-20-2015, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:57:33-07:00","id":596864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=559339#post559339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If people were trying to enslave need and my family I'd get bitter and nasty fighting them. The sidhe came as imperialists and conquistidores, they pretended to no mercy or decency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My point was the selfish and dangerous ways they treat even each other. House Gwydion turned House Leanhaun into a weapon to destroy the world, and did so on a whim. And if you put Arthur Pendragon on a throne and made him King of America I would still take up arms against him. I love the tales of Arthur, but absolute monarchs don't belong in the modern world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The problem is that the dreams of childhood can cripple you as an adult. Monarchy and the dream of the <b>Good King</b> failed, and they still fail. Would you want to live in North Korea? Saudi Arabia? The Commoners moved on, now they are stagnated against their wills.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, monarchy would only be considered bad depending on the culturual norms in which the society is built. In the old world, nobles were groomed from childhood to be leaders. They were educated and experienced at handling the pressures of leading a city, a kingdom, a country. You know what happens when you have one person calling the shots?<br /> <br /> Shit gets done. Out of all the societies that have existed in human history, the only two I could name who pioneered democracy were the Greeks and America, and I'm pretty sure the whole world thinks we Americans are a bunch of dimwitted, money grubbing tyrants. Democracy sounds good on paper, everybody has a valid opinion and an equal chance to govern themselves. But when you have millions of people voicing millions of ideas and nobody can come to an agreement, you have only chaos and ineptitude.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, history is filled with monarchs and conquerors who seized power by force and birthright. They built grand empires and commissioned wondrous architecture or great works of art. Their names became immortalized in stories and even the film industry. They became legends that are still talked about and even admired centuries after their deaths.<br /> <br /> So actually, the Sidhe do have a point. Yeah, following orders without question isn't a life that most people in today's world would voluntarily choose to submit to, but it is a more efficient way to do things than having everybody sit in court and argue for decades on how to solve a problem which grows worse over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:33:16-07:00","id":597095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=596214#post596214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I'm not european. I'm south american.<br /> <br /> Second, I said my frame of reference.<br /> <br /> Third, I'm just saying you can't use any of this to put everyone on the same bag. And you're still doing that.<br /> <br /> Forth, you're starting to do that not against fictional elfs, but against real people here, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your attack was against me and my nation, so I got heated. But surely, what Latin American, given your continent's history wants arbitrary government? Personal rule and elites immune to the rule of law meant that most of your first century of independence was lost time bullied by dictators or by European powers collecting their debts. You guys also tended to see US as something to get loans from and then forget. The Sidhe, as the embodiment of the &quot;Beautiful People&quot; and the &quot;Idle Rich,&quot; should be ugly to you guys as well. The selfish dreams the Sidhe represent poison the will and corrupt ideas. Each of the other Kiths seems to be born of better dreams. Eshu are born of dreams of travel and adventure. Bogans are born of dreams of home and hearth. Poohkas of dreams of freedom and joy. Nockers of the joys and fustraitions of creativity. Sluaghs from our fascination with the night. Satyrs from are passions of both body and mind. Trolls from humanities righteous anger. Red Caps, well they are born of bitterness and rage, but not selfishness.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe are the greatest horror because they are the living force of corruption in the heart of our ideas and dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-20-2015, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:43:14-07:00","id":597109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=596864#post596864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, monarchy would only be considered bad depending on the culturual norms in which the society is built. In the old world, nobles were groomed from childhood to be leaders. They were educated and experienced at handling the pressures of leading a city, a kingdom, a country. You know what happens when you have one person calling the shots?<br /> <br /> Shit gets done. Out of all the societies that have existed in human history, the only two I could name who pioneered democracy were the Greeks and America, and I'm pretty sure the whole world thinks we Americans are a bunch of dimwitted, money grubbing tyrants. Democracy sounds good on paper, everybody has a valid opinion and an equal chance to govern themselves. But when you have millions of people voicing millions of ideas and nobody can come to an agreement, you have only chaos and ineptitude.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, history is filled with monarchs and conquerors who seized power by force and birthright. They built grand empires and commissioned wondrous architecture or great works of art. Their names became immortalized in stories and even the film industry. They became legends that are still talked about and even admired centuries after their deaths.<br /> <br /> So actually, the Sidhe do have a point. Yeah, following orders without question isn't a life that most people in today's world would voluntarily choose to submit to, but it is a more efficient way to do things than having everybody sit in court and argue for decades on how to solve a problem which grows worse over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the same one commoners faced in 14th century England. Nobles assume that everybody's duty is to uphold the Nobles and give up their dreams to the whims of the Nobles. That's why their was a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peasants%27_Revolt\" target=\"_blank\">Peasant's Revolt </a> at the same time as the Sidhe deserted the Earth. Oh and here's a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_peasant_revolts\" target=\"_blank\">list of revolts</a> by peasant's against their noble lords. The Sidhe don't have a Thallain, they are both kith and Thallain in one package of sugared corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-20-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:00:26-07:00","id":597125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=597095#post597095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sidhe are the greatest horror because they are the living force of corruption in the heart of our ideas and dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the sidhe can and do often embody that. they also embody the ideal of chivilry, honor, passion, noble sacrifice, beauty, duty, and leadership.yes, that can twisted and horrific, but it can also be inspiring, just, compassionate and fair. the kith as a whole are not about conquest, oppression, and tyranny like you're making them sound.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:45:47-07:00","id":597498,"title":"","content":"Last time.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about democracy. And I DO support democracy, just for the record.<br /> <br /> The topic should be about a game. I tried to use some real-life exemples but failed, as I expected, and I'm sorry for that.<br /> <br /> Didn't wanted to attack anyone. If you perceived an attack where none existed or I did one without wanting, is moot now. Just sorry.<br /> <br /> You could also stop to talk about Europe, South America, or any other place, people or culture. Please.<br /> <br /> But I do not agree on any level that the worst nightmare should be defined by real-world ideologies.<br /> <br /> Sidhe are dreams of nobility, in all its means. Take from that what you want. If you fear them, your problem. I'm free enough to not.<br /> <br /> Now I'm leaving, this entire thread is nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-21-2015, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T10:55:06-07:00","id":598536,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Astromancer;n597095]<br /> <br /> Each of the other Kiths seems to be born of better dreams. Eshu are born of dreams of travel and adventure. Bogans are born of dreams of home and hearth. Poohkas of dreams of freedom and joy. Nockers of the joys and fustraitions of creativity. Sluaghs from our fascination with the night. Satyrs from are passions of both body and mind. Trolls from humanities righteous anger. Red Caps, well they are born of bitterness and rage, but not selfishness.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Astromancer;n597095]<br /> <br /> So, pretty much, to your way of thinking, all Sidhe are Unseelie, as are all Red Caps, but the rest are all 100% Seelie and embody none of the negative aspects of those dreams?<br /> <br /> Eshu and Pookas can't be the adventurers who leave behind those who need them? They can't be those who watch and delight in others suffering as a tourist?<br /> Bogans can't be manipulative and controlling, binding people to them by chains of need and guilt with swift and cruel punishment mixed with passive-aggressive control manuvers?<br /> Nockers can't be those who build things to maim and twist and hurt because they LIKE doing that and LIKE seeing those things used?<br /> Satyrs can't be passion run amok to the point of abuse? Dark Satyrs are so dark they need a &quot;Do no go here without REALLY talking this over with your players&quot; warning label. Addressing rape shouldn't be a casual thing and, yup, that's what bad satyrs do.<br /> Trolls can't be the implacable guardians that set up impossible standards then viciously kill those who don't measure up. (Really? What's the toll to cross your bridge? I have to give you the right answer or you will kill and eat me?&quot;<br /> <br /> Red Caps.... well, if you've given over righteous indignation to the trolls, you are pretty much left with them being pretty much all bad. The few that aren't are reminiscent of the trope of &quot;fighting the monster inside you to TRY and be good&quot; and that's about it.<br /> <br /> But to categorize the Sidhe as being JUST the bad things you say they are, then to exalt the virtues of the other kiths and ignore their dark sides, particularly when both sides are EXPLICITLY addressed in the <i><b>mechanics </b></i>of the game... it just seems like putting on sun-glasses with a single vertical slot and reading everything so it all comes out just exactly the way you want it to. <br /> <br /> Of course the Sidhe are the worst thing in the world if that's what you want them to be and ignore all evidence to the contrary. <br /> <br /> I don't think that was what Changeling was meant to be about. More &quot;the long slow death of wonder&quot; than &quot;we REALLY HATE all the people who sat at the cool kids table in high school&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T14:24:40-07:00","id":598673,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm pretty sure the metaplot was that humanity was losing its imagination and ability to dream of possibilities, which caused the Fae to slowly die off. It's the whole reason they merged with humans in the first place, to help rekindle their imagination. The Sidhe are ass holes, but so are the Black Spiral Dancers, the Sabbat and more. They are a villain to be sure, but they are not the main premise of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T14:37:01-07:00","id":598678,"title":"","content":"Remember, Red Caps EAT people. Hell, they eat people while they are still ALIVE. They eat CHILDREN while they are still alive. That's not just &quot;bitterness and rage&quot;; it's not some literary metaphorical cannibalism-as-metaphor, that's full on Sawney Bean. And that's not some weird Thallain look-at-twisted-us-in-a-dark-mirror version of Red Caps, that's your typical Unseelie Red Cap (which means your typical Red Cap). <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how mincing around, being bossy and pouting when your don't get your way stacks up against cannibalism (vivi-cannibalism?). Oh wait. I DO know. They aren't even comparable. <br /> <br /> Hell, as far as the &quot;villain-o-meter&quot; goes, Sidhe intrinsically don't even stack up with your average &quot;No, I don't want to drink blood, take it all back!&quot; self-hating vampire (who is still drinking blood and probably frenzying and killing prey and then embracing it or some such nonsence... ) or junior woodchuck werewolves (since werewolves are heroes to exactly themselves and out of control unkillable cuisinart fucking monsters to everyone else.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T21:58:21-07:00","id":599031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=595836#post595836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . One of the most toxic things in my nation is the way so many people in the South (I live in North Carolina and am descended both from slaveholders and abolitionists) hold onto a fantasy about the antebellum south. An anti-democratic fantasy much like that of the sidhe with their chivalric delusions. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading through your posts, I think you're getting hung up on the nature of the changelings, and the Dreaming in general. The fae aren't, and never were human. Broadly speaking, they're living out, over and over again, the stories that humanity has dreamed for them.<br /> <br /> As a result, the fae - any of the fae (not just sidhe) - are capable of both great evil and great good. A sidhe born of the myth of the Good King will <i>be</i> the Good King: wise as Solomon, brave as Arthur, willing to die for the least of his subjects. Particularly for a non-Scathach sidhe, there's no humanity (or human soul) to water that down, or be corrupted. Every action of such a sidhe will be in accordance with every hope and dream humanity has every had for a leader.<br /> <br /> Real world mythology is full of legends about heroic nobles and aristocrats. Horatio at the bridge, where a lone aristocrat fought to the death against an army, all to protect Rome. Roland, the warrior bishop, during the reign of Charlemagne . . . Heck, the stories about the Founding Fathers (of the American Revolution) may well have spawned a sidhe or two . . . &quot;I cannot tell a lie&quot; . . .<br /> <br /> Of course, not every story has a happy ending. And any good story needs villains to oppose, monsters to slay, dark fortresses to storm . . . So when a fae (or freehold) goes bad, they go <i>really </i>evil. The boggan servant, who betrays and murders the &quot;Good King&quot; sidhe who saved him as a child, all for a few bucks. The troll who decides to turn a preschool into a snack bar (remember, Unseelie trolls are called &quot;ogres&quot; for a reason . . . ) The nocker, who decides that Jigsaw (from <i>Saw</i>) had the right idea, and starts trying to &quot;fix' humans with his diabolic machines. . .<br /> <br /> Does that let evil sidhe off the hook? No . . . and doing so would be missing the point. But as long as humans believe that good will triumph in the end, the damage they can do is limited - which limits their ability to be horrific, keeping it (reasonably) localized. Which prevents them from being the greatest horror (particularly since in many places, the Commoners pushed back hard).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If, as the play says, &quot;I dreams begin responsibility.&quot; then the Sidhe are a total abdication of responsibility on all levels. Much like the 14th century English lords that were the models of the Sherriff of Notingham, the Sidhe can't see why their desires aren't seen as normal, good and fine. Just as the nobles saw the rebellious peasants as inspired by the devil, so the Sidhe can only see the commoners as warped or sick. Just like the 19th century slave-holders who saw the desire of their slaves to run away as a mental illness, or present day Europeans like yourself who see all Americans who don't want to ritually humiliated 24/7 as right-wing goons, you avoid seeing that the critique has a point.<br /> <br /> The great horror of the Sidhe is the basis of tragedy, the moral blindness of good people. The Seelie Sidhe do have high ideals, but because they can not see that they are hundreds of years out of step with the times and that aristocracy is no longer valuable, this makes them promotes great evils because of a basic blindness. Just as the standard European view of Americans as worthless Nazi trash poisons the possibility of trans-Atlantic communication. </div> </div> </div>Again, I think you're missing the point of the sidhe. Yes, there are reckless and irresponsible sidhe. Quite a few are outright evil. But they're there for the &quot;good guy&quot; sidhe, or heroic commoner changelings, to take down or redeem. A story where everyone's good, happy, and wealthy is usually quite boring, after all.<br /> <br /> And sure, there are sidhe who don't <i>get</i> the whole &quot;democracy&quot; and &quot;human rights&quot; thing - the intro to <b>Nobles: the Shining Host</b> was written by one, after all. But by definition, a good guy sidhe has to care about the commoners, his story &quot;DNA&quot; requires that he be a good leader to them. If that means giving them a constitution, or a parliament, or rule-of-law courts . . . that's what he'll do.<br /> <br /> Now, you could get some good stories out of the &quot;moral blindness of good people&quot; - a staple of stories since . . . <b>Oedipus Rex </b>or so. But the sidhe don't just play aristocrats in the Dreaming - what they are requires that they live their lives (even the mundane parts) as befits their ancestral story. The brave firefighter who races into a five alarm fire to save an old lady or little kid is very much a staple of the sidhe, as is the charismatic nihilist who leads a band of anarchists in city-wide riots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: On a side note, given how popular (and inspired) &quot;Lost Cause&quot; literature was, I wouldn't be surprised to find a <i>Gone with the Wind</i>-themed freehold or two. Heck, I'd be surprised if there <i>wasn't</i> a chimerical Tara or two out there. Changelings build with dreams, after all.<br /> <br /> But by the same token, most of the famed sites from the Civil Rights movement (at least those not claimed by other supernaturals) have probably been turned into freeholds, too. The dream of freedom is one of the most potent, after all. And it wouldn't be the first - the site of the Liberty Tree is now a well-know freehold in Boston (The Fool's Gambit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  typo 07-22-2015, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:57:27-07:00","id":599639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=556885#post556885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just blatant propaganda, especially when you realize that most of the horrors the book describes being committed with Sovereign are actually impossible to do with Sovereign.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was wrong with the use of Sovereign in Fool's Luck? (Has never used it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:40:22-07:00","id":599664,"title":"","content":"It explicitly can not be used for anything that would cause self harm.<br /> <br /> Geas may be used to assign someone a task that they're not expect to survive, but actual self harm is right out. The sob story about the pooka who was forced to beat herself every time she thought ill of the sidhe is spelled out as being impossible in Sovereign's write up. It even uses the example of stabbing or cutting one's self as not being allowed by Sovereign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:58:53-07:00","id":599679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=599664#post599664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It explicitly can not be used for anything that would cause self harm.<br /> <br /> Geas may be used to assign someone a task that they're not expect to survive, but actual self harm is right out. The sob story about the pooka who was forced to beat herself every time she thought ill of the sidhe is spelled out as being impossible in Sovereign's write up. It even uses the example of stabbing or cutting one's self as not being allowed by Sovereign.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was more likely the author's mistake than the Character's lie. The Sidhe really do think they are owed unlimited love and respect. No matter what they do. Most bullies see themselves as the victim, poor little me. The Sidhe are , according to the game setting, somewhat unable to see that other people are also people, that they live and feel.<br /> <br /> One critic of historical films complained that the heroes always act like modern people and the villains act like the people did back the period when the film was set. The reason the Sidhe are a great horror is that they act like the archaic aristocrats they are. They aren't monsters because they are evil, they are monsters because they were raised and trained to be monsters. As I pointed out before, the moral blindness of good people is the greatest force of or for evil around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-07-2023, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:41:32-07:00","id":599874,"title":"","content":"You're still painting with overly broad brushes. The sidhe are a PC type - one of the nine core kiths on the same level as trolls, pooka, eshu, boggans, sluagh, nockers, redcaps, and satyrs. They all have the same options, same nuance, and same potential for heroism and villainy.<br /> <br /> If they were meant as the game's big bad, they'd be in the back in the antagonist section along with autumn people and dauntain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T17:26:51-07:00","id":599999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=599664#post599664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It explicitly can not be used for anything that would cause self harm.<br /> <br /> Geas may be used to assign someone a task that they're not expect to survive, but actual self harm is right out. The sob story about the pooka who was forced to beat herself every time she thought ill of the sidhe is spelled out as being impossible in Sovereign's write up. It even uses the example of stabbing or cutting one's self as not being allowed by Sovereign.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could argue that a character who already engages in self-harm might be made to cause self-harm with a clever use of Sovereign, given that it's already part of their behaviour and not necessarily something they'd see as 'harm' over 'a control mechanism'. You'd have to push the character's buttons in the right way, but the result might be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T20:13:00-07:00","id":600141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=599999#post599999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could argue that a character who already engages in self-harm might be made to cause self-harm with a clever use of Sovereign, given that it's already part of their behaviour and not necessarily something they'd see as 'harm' over 'a control mechanism'. You'd have to push the character's buttons in the right way, but the result might be the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could certainly argue that, but then you are using very specific circumstances with a very specific victim in mind. That shouldn't apply to how a power, in general, works.<br /> <br /> I do think it is more likely a writers mistake, but since there is no knowing for sure, how its written has to be how it is taken.<br /> <br /> And just to throw my 2 cents in here, I agree that Sidhe can and do run a full spectrum of character concepts and certainly aren't default antagonists for the setting. Sidhe are not the greatest horror in the setting. Not by a long shot. Others have already explained in greater detail why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:37:47-07:00","id":600711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=599874#post599874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> If they were meant as the game's big bad, they'd be in the back in the antagonist section along with autumn people and dauntain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meant as the big bad and the obvious choice to be the big bad are two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:54:27-07:00","id":600722,"title":"","content":"To quote Atomic Robo, &quot;<a href=\"http://www.atomic-robo.com/atomicrobo/v4ch3-page-20\" target=\"_blank\">Okay, we're done here.</a>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 07-23-2015, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T18:27:35-07:00","id":602408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=600711#post600711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meant as the big bad and the obvious choice to be the big bad are two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad that works for your games. It's not the intention of any incarnation of <b>Changeling</b>, including the upcoming 20th anniversary edition, but it'll still be possible. One of the things we talked about in brainstorming, incidentally, was how to present the sidhe so that they <i>have</i> some obvious redeeming value to other fae and in the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:28:08-07:00","id":603060,"title":"","content":"As a suggestion. Apart from exploring alternate concepts that vary from the stereotype (which it's very important), it might be a good idea to present the Shide (even Traditionalist ones) as people that really 'get things done'.<br /> <br /> All that talk about &quot;protecting their subjects&quot; that has been poured here and there it's pointless if the average Shide it's presented as a haughty rich boy that sits in the freehold and does nothing but give orders and pursue romance.<br /> <br /> If nobles really make an effort to help and empower all Changeling, instead of just sitting there and having an effect on the Dreaming, while taking credit of having opened a lot of freeholds that they didn't open, then somebody might understand why someone might be a Traditionalist commoner without being a fool, anachronistic, or being bullied into submission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T22:18:45-07:00","id":603504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=602408#post602408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . One of the things we talked about in brainstorming, incidentally, was how to present the sidhe so that they <i>have</i> some obvious redeeming value to other fae and in the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Good guy&quot; sidhe are born of the myths of white knights and other champions of good. Isn't being a living legend (and compelled to act as such) &quot;redeeming&quot; enough? We're talking about beings who have a daily to-do list that includes everything from feeding stray cats to slaying demon lords. . . and you want <i>more</i>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T02:47:46-07:00","id":603696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=602408#post602408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Glad that works for your games. It's not the intention of any incarnation of <b>Changeling</b>, including the upcoming 20th anniversary edition, but it'll still be possible. One of the things we talked about in brainstorming, incidentally, was how to present the sidhe so that they <i>have</i> some obvious redeeming value to other fae and in the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, step one? The way the Accordance War was written presents the Sidhe as faceless, dastardly, inhuman oppressors who decided to kill off a LOT of commoners out of nothing more than an undeserved sense of entitlement. I'd suggest a &quot;nobody is innocent&quot; beginning to the war, and to make the Night of Iron Knives a little more... murky. These scenarios are painted as EXTREMELY black-and-white, where the commoners are gormless flawless good guys and the sidhe are scheming ne'er-do-well monsters.<br /> <br /> And then you can play a Sidhe if you want to, yay!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T14:18:15-07:00","id":604181,"title":"","content":"Well, it's an oversimplification for sure, but essentially people generally hate the pretty folks. Just like they hate the elves in any random fantasy setting, or for example the toreadors in VtM. Because they are somewhat idealized humans. They are the rich, and pretty, and social, and gracious and most magical, with the highest culure and longest history etc. And nobody's like to be reminded that he is the ugly duckling. Or the stable boy of the local landlord.<br /> <br /> And well, yes every pointy-ear is a self-indulgent, opressive bastard, as every not-so-shiny commoner is an altruistic, righteus hero. Oh, wait, no, they aren't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T17:32:29-07:00","id":604333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=604181#post604181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's an oversimplification for sure, but essentially people generally hate the pretty folks. Just like they hate the elves in any random fantasy setting, or for example the toreadors in VtM. Because they are somewhat idealized humans. They are the rich, and pretty, and social, and gracious and most magical, with the highest culure and longest history etc. And nobody's like to be reminded that he is the ugly duckling. Or the stable boy of the local landlord.<br /> <br /> And well, yes every pointy-ear is a self-indulgent, opressive bastard, as every not-so-shiny commoner is an altruistic, righteus hero. Oh, wait, no, they aren't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. It's more that some people just despise unearned privilege (especially when it only perpetuates more unearned privilege at the expense of equal opportunities).<br /> <br /> The sidhe are no more inherently worthy of rule than anyone. The right to rule should be earned and decided by the people who will be ruled over. <br /> <br /> That's the perspective of the commoners, at any rate. It's about democracy versus monarchism. In a Western, contemporary culture, monarchism has traditional appeal, but democracy has popular appeal. That's why there's a conflict. But the perspective you describe is probably one many sidhe have about the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T18:33:55-07:00","id":604376,"title":"","content":"&quot;But the perspective you describe is probably one many sidhe have about the situation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yup, that was the intent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And sure, you're right about unearned privilege. It's annoying as hell and I dislike it as the next person, probably more. I prefer the underdog all the time (hence I love WoD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). But in my observation (and that's absolutely not a representative survey) folks really tend to dislike elves in general (I think the common fantasy clich\u00e9 can be applied here) because they indeed often pictured as idealized humans since Tolkien. And moreover they often rub it under the nose of everyone else all the freakin' time. They're elitist uppish assholes quite often and in the surface they have the right to be...<br /> <br /> But in the end a person is just a person.<br /> <br /> In my mind, the bigger question about the sidhe is that the power corrupts idea is very established in human thought and rightly. As the sidhe born from the human dreams of rulers, maybe the corruption within the majority of them is, well, ingrained. It's not a justification, just an observation. The pretties are asses, because they rule, and people tend to think that the rulers are generally asses except a few paragon minority. It's somewhat a catch-22.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T12:24:28-07:00","id":604901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=602408#post602408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Glad that works for your games. It's not the intention of any incarnation of <b>Changeling</b>, including the upcoming 20th anniversary edition, but it'll still be possible. One of the things we talked about in brainstorming, incidentally, was how to present the sidhe so that they <i>have</i> some obvious redeeming value to other fae and in the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. That was always a problem. they never really made a case for why the Sidhe where anything but tyrants, bullies, and twits. If they could make a case for the Sidhe, or at least have a large percentage of the sidhe see their patents of nobility as a ritual/cultural thing, and embrace modern democracy, it would be a serious improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T19:05:51-07:00","id":605182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=604901#post604901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If they could make a case for the Sidhe, or at least have a large percentage of the sidhe see their patents of nobility as a ritual/cultural thing, and embrace modern democracy, it would be a serious improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be the Sidhe succumbing to Winter and letting the dreams they represent die. A world with no noblesse oblige, but also one with no nobility of purpose or honor. And all those other things that people have pointed out again and again and again again that the Sidhe represent that is just as well documented in the Changeling books as much, if not more, than the &quot;horrors&quot; you are describing. (When having the mean popular kids at school be mean to you and keep you down is measure of &quot;horror&quot;, I have a hard time using that word.)<br /> <br /> Just like getting all the Eshu to agree to settled down and stop moving around, wasting time and resources. Putting themselves into danger. Having them learn to be content to stay in one place and stop having adventures. You know, getting rid of all the people who seek out the new and exciting thing the world has to offer, but we also get all the ghoulish glee of watching the travails of others, a la the paparazzi. And it's SOOOOOOOO worth getting rid of the paparazzi to destroy all dreams of exciting adventure, right?<br /> <br /> The problem is that you absolutely will not, at any point, see any POV on the Sidhe other than the one you're espousing. I don't see where you've made your case in any way stronger than your opposition, and, in fact, it really seems to fall flat.<br /> <br /> It seems like another one of those tired &quot;Hate the Man&quot; situations in WoD. It could just as easily be &quot;The Ventrue are the Greatest Horror of Vampire&quot;, &quot;The Order of Hermes/New World Order are the greatest Horror of Mage&quot;, &quot;The Silver Fangs are the greatest Horror of Werewolf&quot;, Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T19:10:22-07:00","id":605183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=604901#post604901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. That was always a problem. they never really made a case for why the Sidhe where anything but tyrants, bullies, and twits. If they could make a case for the Sidhe, or at least have a large percentage of the sidhe see their patents of nobility as a ritual/cultural thing, and embrace modern democracy, it would be a serious improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm just curious if I understand this correctly. The only way for the Sidhe to be redeemable is if they embrace modern democracy? There are many different way to govern which don't involve tyrants and bullies. The Sidhe are literally born of dreams of rulers and there are certainly dreams of benevolent Monarchs. There are plenty of stories in the real world, and several represented in Changeling. I guess I just don't understand why &quot;modern democracy&quot; is being cited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T00:05:09-07:00","id":605346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=605182#post605182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they could make a case for the Sidhe, or at least have a large percentage of the sidhe see their patents of nobility as a ritual/cultural thing, and embrace modern democracy, it would be a serious improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be the Sidhe succumbing to Winter and letting the dreams they represent die. A world with no noblesse oblige, but also one with no nobility of purpose or honor. And all those other things that people have pointed out again and again and again again that the Sidhe represent that is just as well documented in the Changeling books as much, if not more, than the &quot;horrors&quot; you are describing. (When having the mean popular kids at school be mean to you and keep you down is measure of &quot;horror&quot;, I have a hard time using that word.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And there would be consequences. The sidhe are living legends, after all, born in the image of the humans who dreamed them. And if literal white knights and heroes right of myth cannot triumph in the World of Darkness, what hope do mere mortals have?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobles: the Shining Host, p. 83-84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Sidhe Prepare for War</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> If there is a force for good in the World of Darkness, the Seelie fae nobility are a strong part of it. Nor are they passive in their desire to change the world for the better. The sidhe are an inherently powerful, if still formative, force in the modern world. The last few decades have been spent getting their bearings and &quot;taking stock&quot;. This process is almost at a close. The sidhe are now prepare to take a far more active role in the world's affairs. The mood among many nobles is an optimistic [. . . ] call to arms.<br /> <br /> The sidhe are everything that the dark forces of the world wish people to believe they can no longer be. They are, for the most part, kindly, honest, genteel, and brave. Even in the absence of their memories (and much of their old power), they still have the will, the power, and the leadership abilities to blast much of the darkness back to whence it came. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>All it takes is the right sidhe, in the right place, at the right time. One lone sidhe, taking up arms against the darkness. One lone hero, ready to fight and die for his people.<br /> <br /> Ten will follow in his footsteps..<br /> <br /> A hundred will follow the path of the Ten.<br /> <br /> Ten thousand will follow the road blazed by the Hundred.<br /> <br /> Ten times ten thousand will march after the Ten Thousand.<br /> <br /> An army of armies will go to war.<br /> <br /> Humanity will look around at itself, and realize that it is strong. And the Darkness itself will tremble in fear.<br /> <br /> All that may seem far-fetched, particularly in the World of Darkness. But that is what &quot;heroic&quot; sidhe <i>are</i>. The dragon slayers of old. The great champions against the Darkness. Leaders who can raise up even the most broken down populace, and make them strong again. Heroes that draw a line in the sand, and bellow to the oncoming hordes, &quot;You! Shall! Not! Pass!&quot;<br /> <br /> They are one of the great strengths of humanity, long thought lost to the world. And now that they've returned, humanity has a fighting chance. First up on the sidhe target list? Pentex and the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> The only question is . . . does humanity still believe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that you absolutely will not, at any point, see any POV on the Sidhe other than the one you're espousing. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair to <b>Astromancer</b>, it <i>is</i> a canon viewpoint from the game, espoused by the Ranters (an anti-monarchial faction). Granted, its a minority of a minority .. . but it was in there<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T10:51:40-07:00","id":605701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=605182#post605182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would be the Sidhe succumbing to Winter and letting the dreams they represent die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some dreams need to die. Absolute Monarchy, or even constitutional Monarchy were the Monarch has real political power, is a dream that has no valid place in the world. Power without responsibility is evil, or at least must become evil. The Sidhe are a medieval dream, lazily reinforced by a lack of imagination. Monarchy and Aristocracy failed because they simply couldn't fuction in the modern world without becoming brutally repressive or trivial. The Sidhe are trapped on either the path of bedlam or banality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A world with no noblesse oblige, but also one with no nobility of purpose or honor. And all those other things that people have pointed out again and again and again again that the Sidhe represent that is just as well documented in the Changeling books as much, if not more, than the &quot;horrors&quot; you are describing. (When having the mean popular kids at school be mean to you and keep you down is measure of &quot;horror&quot;, I have a hard time using that word.) </div> </div> </div>Honor is an external image of how your worth/virtue is seen by others. Honor killings involve people butchering their loved ones to preserve their honor. The idea of stabing my sister to death because &quot;honor demands it&quot; is a brutal vision of horror in my book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just like getting all the Eshu to agree to settled down and stop moving around, wasting time and resources. Putting themselves into danger. Having them learn to be content to stay in one place and stop having adventures. You know, getting rid of all the people who seek out the new and exciting thing the world has to offer, but we also get all the ghoulish glee of watching the travails of others, a la the paparazzi. And it's SOOOOOOOO worth getting rid of the paparazzi to destroy all dreams of exciting adventure, right? </div> </div> </div>The Eshu don't need to push other people around to be themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that you absolutely will not, at any point, see any POV on the Sidhe other than the one you're espousing. I don't see where you've made your case in any way stronger than your opposition, and, in fact, it really seems to fall flat. </div> </div> </div>What you're saying is that the Sidhe can't grow to be more or better than they are. They represent a dream that can't be part of the modern world without poisoning it. Dreams like <b><i>Racial Purity, World Conquest, Monarchy, Civilizing Missions, A Universal World Religion,</i></b> or <b><i> Aristocracy</i></b> have no valid place in the modern world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like another one of those tired &quot;Hate the Man&quot; situations in WoD. It could just as easily be &quot;The Ventrue are the Greatest Horror of Vampire&quot;, &quot;The Order of Hermes/New World Order are the greatest Horror of Mage&quot;, &quot;The Silver Fangs are the greatest Horror of Werewolf&quot;, Etc. </div> </div> </div>It's not &quot;I Hate the Man.&quot; It's the dream the sidhe represent is sick. To retain their unjust rule they bring banality and bedlam in their wake. Beautiful they are, and many, even many of the most monsterous, can be well intended. But they need to force the world into reinforcing their dream at the expense of human creativity and freedom. For the Sidhe to thrive humanity must give up all dreams except those that feed the sidhe. We must cast away democracy, justice, and freedom, in exchange for the honor of those that can never see us as anything but cheap toys.<br /> <br /> Either let the sidhe move on to new dreams, or let them pass into storybooks and be placed on the shelf. The other changeling moved with the times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-02-2025, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T11:16:57-07:00","id":605735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=605183#post605183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm just curious if I understand this correctly. The only way for the Sidhe to be redeemable is if they embrace modern democracy? There are many different way to govern which don't involve tyrants and bullies. The Sidhe are literally born of dreams of rulers and there are certainly dreams of benevolent Monarchs. There are plenty of stories in the real world, and several represented in Changeling. I guess I just don't understand why &quot;modern democracy&quot; is being cited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it's as simple as the Sidhe might redeem themselves if they switched from wanting to be kings and nobles, and enforcing a toxic dead paradigm, to being leaders and champions. Leaders are needed in any society, King isn't the only model of leader out there. Knights were basically bullies and thugs. Modern sidhe champions could embrace roles like firemen, police officers, forest rangers, EMTs, and others people who protect and serve the community. Is the firefighter less worthy than the knight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T11:19:53-07:00","id":605737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=605346#post605346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, to be fair to <b>Astromancer</b>, it <i>is</i> a canon viewpoint from the game, espoused by the Ranters (an anti-monarchial faction). Granted, its a minority of a minority .. . but it was in there</div> </div> </div> </div>That could have worked, but when did they do anything to promote that viewpoint? Yes, it sounded good when I read that passage years ago. But in near twenty years where is any follow-up?<br /> <br /> Note: The real Ranters where heroic commoners (human) that stood up for the rights of the common people. Which is why they are still loathed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-28-2015, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T15:13:32-07:00","id":605991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=605701#post605701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's not &quot;I Hate the Man.&quot; It's the dream the sidhe represent is sick. To retain their unjust rule they bring banality and bedlam in their wake. Beautiful they are, and many, even many of the most monsterous, can be well intended. But they need to force the world into reinforcing their dream at the expense of human creativity and freedom. For the Sidhe to thrive humanity must give up all dreams except those that feed the sidhe. We must cast away democracy, justice, and freedom, in exchange for the honor of those that can never see us as anything but cheap toys.<br /> <br /> Either let the sidhe move on to new dreams, or let them past into storybooks and be placed on the shelf. The other changeling move with the times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Sihe are dreams given sentience, though. They are magical entities who do not function the same way as mortal creatures understand it. When I hear of the Sidhe, I'm reminded of Kingdoms of Amalur, in which the Fae are constantly referred to as manifestations of nature itself, and yet mortals constantly expect them to behave and think like normal people. If a Fae is wild and destructive, it is not because they are evil anymore than a wolf is evil for attacking human travelers near its den, it is because destruction is part of their very nature. It is what they represent, it is what they were born of and denying that nature would be as alien to them as a life without thought would be to a human.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mayhaps the Sidhe would be considered outdated, but that doesn't mean other changelings move with the times. It means they are born from what humans currently dream about and fear, and once humanity dreams and fears something else, then they too shall become outdated and irrelevant. Humans imagination creates the Fae, but humanity's progress and ingenuity are the cause of their deaths, too.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T20:03:33-07:00","id":606280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=605735#post605735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps it's as simple as the Sidhe might redeem themselves if they switched from wanting to be kings and nobles, and enforcing a toxic dead paradigm, to being leaders and champions. Leaders are needed in any society, King isn't the only model of leader out there. Knights were basically bullies and thugs. Modern sidhe champions could embrace roles like firemen, police officers, forest rangers, EMTs, and others people who protect and serve the community. Is the firefighter less worthy than the knight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidhe don't necessarily &quot;want&quot; to be anything. They <u>are</u> kings and nobles. The Dreaming (their World) enforces it. They are also (already) leaders and champions. Real world knights may have been bullies and thugs (though I don't agree all were), but the dreams of Knights and Kings are not. And that's what Sidhe are born of. Can they be &quot;evil&quot; (kind of a useless word in most discussions about the WoD)? Sure. Any Kith can be &quot;evil&quot;. That's kind of built into the system.<br /> <br /> I don't get throwing out terms like &quot;toxic paradigm&quot;. You seem to be adamantly against the setting, and zeroing in on the Sidhe as the cause of it when they are simply one aspect of it.Changeling society is anachronistic. That is the Setting. Also, I've seen multiple Sidhe concepts that pretty much exactly what you are saying the Sidhe <i>should</i> be. I've played in a game with a Sidhe police officer, who was in fact, also a Knight.<br /> <br /> All changelings are beings of 2 worlds. You are saying that the Sidhe need to forsake their role in the Dreaming/setting and embrace the modern world. If this were done by any particular changeling (not just Sidhe), it would be the death of said changeling. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T00:07:15-07:00","id":606401,"title":"","content":"Very true.<br /> <hr />Anycase, I think that if the Shide had a more clear representation in the material as forces that DO good things, then it would be much more understandable that they would be beloved, even being tyrants.<br /> <br /> For instance, if the knight was to murder the redcap that it's about to eat your daugther, you won't mind his murderous ways. Perhaps in the Dreaming dragons are a worse trouble than criminals, and the knights more needed than policeman (which doesn't mean that the Shide can't be a good policeman in real life. It would have all the sense of the world).<br /> <br /> Most people just want to live better, if Shide presence does that for Changelings, then it works as a system. But the setting it's always bent on making them &quot;the Man&quot;, to the point the the &quot;exploits&quot; of Shide knights are more the stuff of legend (and player characters) than something that happens in the setting. For instance, the Shide are reputed to have opened a lot of freeholds, however they didn't, they merely taken the merit for it. To me, that was totally unnecessary. Saying that Shide are noble and heroic it's worthless if they aren't represented doing noble and heroic things.<br /> <br /> If Shide were represented as the page in the manual (as kind, wise, and more than anything: protectors of their people that want to empower the Changeling) then it would be understandable if they were beloved by commoners. Good Shide should be the first to step when there's trouble, and the first to scheme and plot ways to improve the life of ALL Changelings under his banner (at least their fae life).<br /> Sure, under Shide banner you can't choose your representatives, but if you have Glamour, shelter, and someone that will try to protect you when the RedCaps, unseelie Trolls and other nigthmanres kick the door, having them as absolute monarchs may be a fair trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-29-2015, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T07:15:06-07:00","id":606536,"title":"","content":"Changelings often are evil by human standards. That isn't a flaw in the setting, as it's kind of the point of the oWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T19:06:07-07:00","id":607342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=606536#post606536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings often are evil by human standards. That isn't a flaw in the setting, as it's kind of the point of the oWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Every splat is evil by &quot;human standards,&quot; but the point of WoD isn't to see things from a human perspective. You play the monsters, start thinking like a monster. Granted a monster who's trying not to become a raging psychopath, but acknowledges they do what they do out of necessity to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T19:57:10-07:00","id":607385,"title":"","content":"I don't think the &quot;point&quot; of Changeling it's to play a monster. Changeling it's not vampire, and your character doesn't need to do truly &quot;monstrous&quot; things to survive. You don't need to kill anyone, and even defending absolute monarchy isn't mandatory (albeit I would hardly call that to &quot;be a monster&quot;).<br /> <br /> The fact that you can be a monstrous Changeling doesn't mean that that's the point of the game. Your Changeling can be a very positive force in the WoD. In fact, I think that the &quot;point&quot; of the game it's to be that. <b>Changelings regain Glamour spreading dreams, love and creativity</b>. I would NEVER call that to be a &quot;monster&quot;, even if these creatures happen to dislike democracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T21:11:43-07:00","id":607471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=607385#post607385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the &quot;point&quot; of Changeling it's to play a monster. Changeling it's not vampire, and your character doesn't need to do truly &quot;monstrous&quot; things to survive. You don't need to kill anyone, and even defending absolute monarchy isn't mandatory (albeit I would hardly call that to &quot;be a monster&quot;).<br /> <br /> The fact that you can be a monstrous Changeling doesn't mean that that's the point of the game. Your Changeling can be a very positive force in the WoD. In fact, I think that the &quot;point&quot; of the game it's to be that. <b>Changelings regain Glamour spreading dreams, love and creativity</b>. I would NEVER call that to be a &quot;monster&quot;, even if these creatures happen to dislike democracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are too many kiths that have names of monsters from folklore and fairy tales to discount changelings from the monster club. They can even get a wide array of monsters for pets in the form of chimerae, such as dragons, manticores, etc. Of course, the WoD being what it is, sometimes monsters can do better than humans. It goes hand in hand with some monsters draining the passion from someone for good to dominate petty rivalries in court, redcaps reveling in the reactions they get from eating someone, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T03:09:28-07:00","id":607588,"title":"","content":"It's certainly true that fae are among the least monstrous denizens of the Old World of Darkness, but the original premise of WoD was 'play the monsters'. So it's not totally unreasonable to refer to them as monsters. <br /> <br /> By most definitions, trolls, redcaps, riverhags, boggans, etc, ARE monsters. Often mischievous rather than evil, usually capricious more than malicious, but the whole 'changeling' thing comes from myths of faeries stealing people's babies. Let's not forget that fae literally steal the bodies of humans. Sure, they claim it's fair on the human soul, but the sidhe at least might be doing it by slinging mortal souls into the Dreaming to grab their skin.<br /> <br /> But honestly, let's not derail another thread by arguing the minutiae of semantics? Arguing whether the fae are monstrous or not is pointless, because subjectively everyone will have a different opinion on what a monster is and whether they play or interpret the game that way.<br /> <br /> We were talking about the sidhe. In the real world, they'd be outdated tyrants (there are plenty of these still running our countries in real life, by the way, if you really want to get angry about something worthwhile...). But it's a game. Debating the evilness of fictional character types seems a little odd to me. Call for clarification, yes. But be clear about what you want clarified and move on. If you hate unearned privilege and entitlement, campaign against it in the real world, or roleplay it out in your games, but it seems pointless getting angry about setting fluff. A roleplaying game is meant to set up plot hooks and opportunities for conflict, not to create a setting for us all to roleplay utopia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-30-2015, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:31:55-07:00","id":611277,"title":"","content":"Redcaps and riverhags are mischievous rather than evil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:35:44-07:00","id":612607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=611277#post611277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redcaps and riverhags are mischievous rather than evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. A Seelie redcap needn't be evil. Even an Unseelie one needn't be evil. But evil is subjective in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T16:43:34-07:00","id":612783,"title":"","content":"Then a Shide needn't to be a Tyrant, and the evilness of tyranny it's subjective in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T06:48:35-07:00","id":613310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=612783#post612783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then a Shide needn't to be a Tyrant, and the evilness of tyranny it's subjective in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. /endthread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:01:18-07:00","id":613582,"title":"","content":"Evil is only subjective if you've never been around it. Spend some QT with a serial killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T09:32:22-07:00","id":615217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=613582#post613582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evil is only subjective if you've never been around it. Spend some QT with a serial killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>One man's 'evil' is another man's 'mentally ill' or 'completely relatable'. A serial killer might not think he's evil. Good and evil only have meaning because we give them meaning. They're not universal constants. In the WoD in particular, 'evil' and 'hero' (or at least, 'protagonist') are not mutually exclusive. There's a great continuum of grey. Even the things described or portrayed as evil are shown to have some redeeming qualities (Grandmother, the Wyrm, Caine, Lilith, Lucifer, God?). Usually these things operate at levels where evil is meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:07:09-07:00","id":615321,"title":"","content":"One thing it's seelie Sidhe evil that protect the people without letting them to choose their representatives, and other thing, unseelie Redcap evil that eats your children 'for the lulz'. Mischievous Seelie Pooka it's hardly &quot;evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> Changeling has many evil character roles to chose and play, but also plenty of characters that ain't suggested to be particularly evil, or that are supposed to be just mischievous. That's why I don't think that playing evil it's the 'core' of the game. I don't think that at playing a genuinely good character you're straying from that core. Changeling it's not &quot;about&quot; playing an evil character. <br /> <br /> In contrast, while you can play a good Vampire, you still can frenezy and end killing lot's of innocent people. Playing 'good' in Vampire can be genuinely difficult, and the characters are expected to degenerate eventually. Changeling it's not about turning into a monster, or &quot;playing the monster&quot;, in the same sense as Vampire. The mechanics don't drive you to that extreme (if you go, it's because you want, not because the game it's geared that way)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:03:45-07:00","id":615422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=607588#post607588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But honestly, let's not derail another thread by arguing the minutiae of semantics? Arguing whether the fae are monstrous or not is pointless, because subjectively everyone will have a different opinion on what a monster is and whether they play or interpret the game that way.<br /> <br /> We were talking about the sidhe. In the real world, they'd be outdated tyrants (there are plenty of these still running our countries in real life, by the way, if you really want to get angry about something worthwhile...). But it's a game. Debating the evilness of fictional character types seems a little odd to me. Call for clarification, yes. But be clear about what you want clarified and move on. If you hate unearned privilege and entitlement, campaign against it in the real world, or roleplay it out in your games, but it seems pointless getting angry about setting fluff. A roleplaying game is meant to set up plot hooks and opportunities for conflict, not to create a setting for us all to roleplay utopia.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, every kith has it's monster face. Any and all faerie folk can be monsters, but the Sidhe are in a special trap. The Sidhe need dreams of unjust social structures to thrive. Polkas, good, bad, indifferent, even Beasties, can make do with dreams about animals, or dreaming that you're an animal, heck, even Bugs Bunny cartoons. The Sidhe live on the dream of the &quot;Good King&quot; of monarchies, and traditions that can't be changed, even when they strangle society to death, dreams of privilege, and unearned advantage. Poisoned dreams the world needs to drop.<br /> <br /> This makes them the greatest horror in the game. They are the greatest horror because they are both totally seductive and totally poisonous. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T15:59:58-07:00","id":615673,"title":"","content":"No rule says you can only feed on Glamour through monarchy, if you're a Sidhe. In fact, no rule even sugest that you should feed on royality or on being royal. You can be a perfectly well developed Sidhe without ever enslaving anyone.<br /> <br /> And many Sidhe want to change traditions, it's just that most don't want to change them in such a radical way as to bring democracy (which by itself, isn't a guarantee of happiness, you know)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:24:20-07:00","id":615788,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the fae of Greece have a different political system? I'd like a system with philosopher-kings at the top as an alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:17:27-07:00","id":616561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=615788#post615788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the fae of Greece have a different political system? I'd like a system with philosopher-kings at the top as an alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bought all the <b>C:tD</b> back when they came out. Europe, outside of the British Isles, France, Spain, and the Low countries, is run by a confederation of commoners. It seems to be a syndicalist form of anarchy. Hyper-reactionary Sidhe hold France in a death grip. The Sidhe of France seem to have a mixture of fascism and monarchy with all commoners under mind-warping geas of some kind or other.<br /> <br /> I think this is covered in the Commoner's book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T17:39:38-07:00","id":616952,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I'll re-read it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T07:14:00-07:00","id":617731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=552466#post552466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While certain sidhe could definitely be horrific, I'd hardly call them the central horror of Changeling. The true darkness of Changeling is that no matter what you do, no matter what you accomplish, you are doomed forget it and you're true nature. No one will ever know what kind of life you lived.<br /> <br /> It's actually something that hits me a lot harder these days than when I was playing the game back in its heyday. The past several years I've had to watch as Alzheimer's has slowly taken my grandmother. Now days, her body is there, but she just isn't. Believe me, that's some gut wrenching, horrific stuff, and it's the fate of every single changeling. The lucky ones are the who go out in a blaze of glory fighting some monster or an evil sidhe ruler.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YOU hit it right on the nail PookaKnight. I too am seeing this with my mother. To be forgotten is the worst thing ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T09:33:30-07:00","id":620175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=554874#post554874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidhe. The word is <b>Sidhe</b>. A shide is a thin board.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a Tolkien-ish elf lady and a band <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T10:48:06-07:00","id":622420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=615422#post615422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, every kith has it's monster face. Any and all faerie folk can be monsters, but the Sidhe are in a special trap. <b>The Sidhe need dreams of unjust social structures to thrive.</b> Polkas, good, bad, indifferent, even Beasties, can make do with dreams about animals, or dreaming that you're an animal, heck, even Bugs Bunny cartoons. The Sidhe live on the dream of the &quot;Good King&quot; of monarchies, and traditions that can't be changed, even when they strangle society to death, dreams of privilege, and unearned advantage. Poisoned dreams the world needs to drop.<br /> <br /> This makes them the greatest horror in the game. They are the greatest horror because they are both totally seductive and totally poisonous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monarchies are not inherently unjust. Nor are democracies inherently just.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/423-sapphite","name":"Sapphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:37:30-07:00","id":622469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sapphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=622420#post622420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Monarchies are not inherently unjust. Nor are democracies inherently just.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically, Monarchies need to put hierarchy before anything else. This leads to a need to keep people in line. Injustice is generally the first tool used. Democracies aren't inherently just, that is true, but justice isn't fundamentally a threat in democracy. So, justice is more likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:22:54-07:00","id":622531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=622469#post622469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This leads to a need to keep people in line.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true of any and all governing bodies. I don't see why you are singling out Monarchies.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=622469#post622469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Injustice is generally the first tool used.</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement is entirely opinion and subjective.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=622469#post622469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Democracies aren't inherently just, that is true, but justice isn't fundamentally a threat in democracy. So, justice is more likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also subjective and not terribly true. Justice means different things to different people and so &quot;Justice&quot; has a place in (again) any and all governing bodies. You seem to be making broad sweeping statements that could apply to various forms of government and only thinking of them in terms of how they make the Sidhe look bad.<br /> <br /> At this point I think I will just accept that you dislike any government that isn't your version of a democracy, and that is leading to the unnecessary villainization of the Sidhe. There are a great many in game reasons to think the Sidhe villains. The structure of Changeling society not being a democracy isn't one of them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:08:27-07:00","id":622705,"title":"","content":"&quot;Injustice&quot; it's not a tool, injustice it's a moral statement, perhaps a moral sentiment.<br /> <br /> I would dare say that, since &quot;injustice&quot; usually breeds discontent and rebellion, a monarchy needs to be perceived as &quot;just&quot;. Just, of course, doesn't mean egalitarian. A monarchy it's inherently hierarchical by necessity.<br /> <br /> While I happen to think that democracies have the potential of being a far better system than monarchies (for varied reasons that I won't discuss, but that you may imagine), I also think that a democratic government it's not immune to royally fuck things up, and that if a &quot;monarch&quot; demonstrates that he can do things better, providing the needs of the people while giving enough living space to don't feel suffocated, I wouldn't complain because of a hierarchy.<br /> <br /> That's why, returning to WoD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , I think that the Sidhe need to be able to proof that they deserve to rule. Not only by being just (which seelie Sidhe are supposed to be), but more so,<i> being efficient</i>. Now there are many books that state that the Sidhe can be just and efficient, but this has rarely been a thing in the metaplot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T05:49:38-07:00","id":623230,"title":"","content":"There's another political issue that both commoners and nobles are guilty of, and that's one of colonialism. They went over to the Americas and took the land from the nunnehi in order to set up their own political system (and take all the freeholds for themselves). So, really, the sidhe returning to rule the commoners is no worse than what all of them did to the native fae. I think that potentially counts as at least an equal horror in CTD, but not one most PCs have to deal with, because the perspective is that of the conquerors'. Again: morality, subjective, blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> The problem, I think, isn't really morality but nuance. The sidhe are often stereotypes. The problem with stereotypes isn't that they're untrue, but that they tell only one truth. Hence, they're partial and flawed. Sidhe being heroes or being villains isn't the problem--it's being nothing but heroes or villains, and not occupying any spaces in between. This means one-dimension characterisation and fewer options for players. Well written splats suggest seeds for more rather than fewer characters.<br /> <br /> This is not just a problem with the sidhe, however. To me, the kiths as written appear more restrictive than the splats in other gamelines, but that's just because CTD never went through the Revised-era process of filling in the gaps and presenting a wider range of possibilities for each. This is something I'm sure C20 will rectify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T07:15:32-07:00","id":1520033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sapphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=622420#post622420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Monarchies are not inherently unjust. Nor are democracies inherently just.</div> </div> </div> </div>True as far as you go. But monarchies tend toward injustice because they favor hierarchy at the expense of other possibilities. Democracies aren't automatically good, but they offer more possibilities for good outcomes and more opportunities to challenge entrenched evils. Swimming in deep and turbulent waters is easier in a life vest than with a millstone around your neck. Monarchies are normally millstones, not always of course, but they tend towards Saudi Arabia more than Denmark. Democracies can fail, most do fail, but a hope of justice is far better than a certainty of chains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T08:07:51-07:00","id":1520037,"title":"","content":"So, this thread has been resurrected after nearly eight years. When it was last posted to, the 20th Anniversary Edition was still in the works. It's now 2023, and C20 has been out for a while. <br /> <br /> What has changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T11:25:59-07:00","id":1520047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=1520037#post1520037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this thread has been resurrected after nearly eight years. When it was last posted to, the 20th Anniversary Edition was still in the works. It's now 2023, and C20 has been out for a while.<br /> <br /> What has changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone gave me a like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T11:51:59-07:00","id":1520049,"title":"","content":"I wasn't asking why you resurrected the thread (thought bumping a thread just because someone gave you a like doesn't seen appropriate to me). I was asking, quite literally, this: with the release of C20, <i>what has changed?</i> Are the Sidhe still the ultimate horrors in C20, as you see it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T14:22:05-07:00","id":1520056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=1520049#post1520049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't asking why you resurrected the thread (thought bumping a thread just because someone gave you a like doesn't seen appropriate to me). I was asking, quite literally, this: with the release of C20, <i>what has changed?</i> Are the Sidhe still the ultimate horrors in C20, as you see it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was somewhat exaggerating. But the Sidhe are monsters. The Medieval nobility, which the Sidhe in the game are a reflection of, would be monsters to our modern eyes. The &quot;ards&quot; (literally kings, but used as a generic term for noble) of ancient Ireland were even worse (although they had some surprising virtues). The Sidhe as described in game are fairly brutal. <br /> <br /> House Gwydion, supposed leaders of the Seelie, are fairly ruthless and quick to crush anyone suggesting that political thought has evolved since the 1400s. They're like putting Tory-mossbacks in charge of the United States without allowing any human rights. <br /> <br /> For a group that's supposed to be a force of pure good, they come off as vile. <br /> <br /> Still, in a WoD game, monsters that insist they are becons of light and virtue work. Look at the Planter Elites of the CSA. They presented themselves as a force pure good even as they fought for slavery and racism. To this day much of the world buys into the South's take of the ACW. The Lost Cause Mythology is still popular and in much of the world is the basis of American Civil War history as known to the general public. Similarly the Nazis proclaimed themselves fighting a war against &quot;Asiatic Darkness.&quot; The Stalinists and the Maoists justified the murder of millions because they said they were fighting for humanity's future against Western Imperialism. <br /> <br /> The European Chattering Classes attack America with endless vulgar lies because America is proclaimed corrupt. Once I pointed out to a German woman that, because Germany burned so much lignite (brown coal), her nation put more carbon in the atmosphere than America even though we had four times Germany's population. She said &quot;American carbon always hurts the world more.&quot; She believed what she said, because, like the Sidhe she'd always been told she was one of the good guys and anyone that challenged that was evil.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T14:23:22-07:00","id":1520057,"title":"","content":"What about the distinction that C20 makes between Arcadian Sidhe and Autumn Sidhe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T14:24:24-07:00","id":1520058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/551566-the-greastest-horror-in-changeling?p=1520057#post1520057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the distinction that C20 makes between Arcadian Sidhe and Autumn Sidhe?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting. I need to see what they do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}